Aqueous corrosion — Cambridge DoITPoMS (@mat-aqueous: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_3P6KCGYFDFBG1WYEJ2EZY6G7J5
Noel Rutter and Chris Smith, University of Cambridge. Read the complete [Aqueous Corrosion package](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/aqueous_corrosion/index.php), with questions; the [printable text](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/aqueous_corrosion/printall.php) collects the explanation. Electrochemical reactions, the interface, activation barriers, polarization, diffusion limitation, passivation, rate and control form an accessible first sequence.

The printable text and selected Tafel, transport, passivation and Faraday-law passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. Re-derive equations rather than copying notation: activation Gibbs energy and reaction Gibbs energy have different meanings, and jM/(ρzF) is a thickness-change rate, not a thickness. A print view does not reproduce every film, interactive exercise or answer.

The inspected footer states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with exceptions. Preserve authors and component credits. Readings and media remain external.

**Return:** [Materials-engineering sources — reading and primary evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_51JAH6DB4WV2HZAB69G21ZHSMK).
